Dear Charles,

I have finished reviewing the plans for the Analytical Engine, and I am
convinced it can do far more than calculate tables. With the right sequence of
operations on the punched cards, the machine could manipulate symbols of any
kind — not merely numbers.

A few points I would like to discuss when we next meet:

- The engine might one day compose elaborate pieces of music, if we can encode
  the rules of harmony as operations.
- We should document the operation cards carefully so others can reproduce a
  computation without re-deriving it.
- I have drafted a short program to compute Bernoulli numbers; I will bring it.

It is the analysis of the process, not the mechanism itself, that will prove
most enduring.

Yours in anticipation,
Ada
